      "id": 1,
      "text": "Pine Mountain first appeared on the map in 1882 when a railroad from Columbus arrived, and it was known as Chipley until 1958.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine_Mountain%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town adopted the name Pine Mountain after Callaway Gardens opened, replacing the earlier name Chipley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine_Mountain%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pine Mountain rests at the northern base of the Pine Mountain Range, giving it a unique foothill landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine_Mountain%2C_Georgia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Harris County side of Pine Mountain belongs to the Columbus metropolitan area, while the Meriwether County corner falls under Atlanta’s metro.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pine_Mountain%2C_Georgia"
    },
